    "source": "src/sc_neurocore/neurons/model_schemas/mihalas_niebur.toml",
    "equation": "Driven Mihalas-Niebur generalised integrate-and-fire trace with 36 v>=theta resets. The four-state linear flow dv/dt=(-(v-v_rest)+i1+i2+I)/tau_v, dtheta/dt=(theta_inf-theta+a*(v-v_rest))/tau_theta, di1/dt=-i1/tau_1, di2/dt=-i2/tau_2 is advanced with the classical fourth-order Runge-Kutta step, independently re-derived from Mihalas & Niebur (2009), including the adaptive-threshold reset v=v_reset+b*(v-v_rest), theta=max(theta, theta_reset), i1+=r1, i2+=r2. theta_reset (1.3) exceeds theta_inf (1.0), so the max() threshold floor engages on every spike.",
    "citation": "doi:10.1162/neco.2008.12-07-680"
  },
